WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:04.880
Speaker 1: I do want to take a quick look
at The David Pakman Show sub Reddit.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.050
Find it at David Pakman Dotcom it.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:13.970
Now, more than 31000 of you subscribed to
the sub Reddit.

00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:19.519
Here is a post that I find interesting, and
it's called Sometimes I Fear being judged

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:23.179
for not wearing a mask after being fully vaccinated.

00:00:23.179 --> 00:00:29.169
And this viewer says right now in California,
June 15th, the mask mandate is going away.

00:00:29.169 --> 00:00:30.749
And I'm personally pretty excited for it.

00:00:30.749 --> 00:00:35.200
I was fully vaccinated in March, got my first
dose in February when I randomly got a text

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.059
saying my local vaccination clinic had spare
doses.

00:00:38.059 --> 00:00:39.690
I immediately lined up.

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:43.760
I've been seeing a lot of comments on left
YouTube videos and Subrata saying what the

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.740
CDC did was stupid or we should keep wearing
masks forever because they prevent the flu.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.030
And that kind of worries me.

00:00:50.030 --> 00:00:53.609
Not that I'm judging anyone for continuing
to wear a mask, but that people might decide

00:00:53.609 --> 00:00:58.409
to yell at me or judge me for not wearing
one at a grocery store without a mandate once

00:00:58.409 --> 00:01:00.920
the California mask mandate is gone.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:04.720
I've heard stories in San Francisco of people
getting harassed outdoors for not wearing

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.710
a mask, even though it's been months since
the CDC and California government said it

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:09.760
was OK.

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.370
Do you think people will end up judging me
or seeing me as a Republican if I stop wearing

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:16.050
a mask indoors once the California mandate
is gone?

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:22.380
Yeah, I mean, the truth is some people will
and there's going to be a readjustment period.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:26.900
And I think that people essentially just have
to decide.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:32.740
What is more important to you is the belief
and understanding that the CDC guidelines

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.980
for vaccinated people feel OK to you.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:42.160
More important than the fact that a couple
of people might give you a dirty look because

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.820
you're not wearing a mask.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:45.950
And it's just a very personal decision.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:51.030
As I've said before, I think it's great to
have the possibility of wearing a mask and

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:57.480
for it to be normalized during flu season,
and particularly if not only if if in November,

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:01.740
it starts looking like we're having a heavy
flu season against which I will be vaccinated,

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:05.140
I get my flu vaccine and covid cases start
going up.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:07.940
I will be glad to when I go.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:11.430
I mean, the real place I'm thinking of is
the grocery store or public transit.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.430
I'll be glad to go back to wearing a mask.

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:15.890
I think that that's a great thing.

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:21.370
That being said, right now, with cases so
low, with the variance so well controlled

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:28.260
by the vaccine, by the by all vaccines, I'm
comfortable not wearing a mask outdoors.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:31.780
And when it comes to indoors, just doing what
the location requires.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:35.770
And if they don't require require wearing
a mask, I'm comfortable not doing it.

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:38.590
And is anybody judging me?

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:39.590
Probably.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.860
Probably, but I'm completely comfortable with
it.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:46.840
It's a very personal thing and I think a lot
of it is just personality driven.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:51.920
What what is more important to you saying
there's no reason for me to wear a mask based

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.030
on the medical guidelines.

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:58.060
So I'm not going to regardless of the consequences
or I value more the way that people see me,

00:02:58.060 --> 00:03:00.890
even if it's random people.

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:04.850
That's a very personal decision that really
only you can make for yourself.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.510
Another interesting post on the subhead.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:09.810
It asks, how do you guys stay sane?

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:12.090
I just finished Pakman show from yesterday.

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:14.830
And I've got to say, it's depressing.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:18.790
From gridlock in the Senate to Trump still
having a large base of support, I find myself

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:21.830
so discouraged and turned off by politics
right now.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:28.440
How do you guys keep from being this way going
on to say later, I live and work in a very

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:31.360
conservative area, so I'm inundated with this
stuff all the time.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:34.480
I hear really racist, homophobic things at
work all the time.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:37.690
How do my fellow liberals in conservative
areas cope with the latter part?

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:42.069
I can't answer, but I think it is really healthy.

00:03:42.069 --> 00:03:47.180
To check out from the news for a few days,
every single week when I'm done producing

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:53.440
the Friday show, I do not pay attention to
the news unless something major happens or

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:59.210
unless I stumble across something because
I turn the TV on or look at Facebook.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:04.150
I am checking out of news for almost three
days every week.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:06.790
OK, that's like almost half the week in a
sense.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:08.300
I think it's imperative.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:10.530
I think it's absolutely imperative to maintain
sanity.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:13.910
And I would encourage I would encourage people
to do it.

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:16.250
And then the other thing is.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:22.599
Adopt a bit of stoic philosophy about really
understanding what is within your locus of

00:04:22.599 --> 00:04:28.100
control and what is not, because there are
always things to be upset about, because so

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:30.229
many upsetting things are happening.

00:04:30.229 --> 00:04:34.810
But to some degree, understanding the limits,
can we activate about something and try to

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:36.280
influence a political issue?

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:37.280
Great.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:38.280
Let's do it.

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:42.159
But understand that you can't control the
outcomes of everything that's happening.

00:04:42.159 --> 00:04:46.180
And to some degree, we've got to continue
living our lives and making the best we can

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.180
of them.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:48.699
So I think that that would be my advice.

00:04:48.699 --> 00:04:52.389
But I'm right there with you two really good
posts today.

00:04:52.389 --> 00:04:56.749
Make your own post and maybe it'll make it
onto the show next week on the sub.

